From a5dde5ed89b6ab7dc5323d9a22273b208e662b0a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Fri, 31 Jul 2026 12:29:29 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 08054/11362] Independently replicated: the empty intersection
 was the depth cap -- and 21 of 40 stall candidates never had a working engine
 at all

Phase 2 asked why the stall path has never cleared the goal gate in 22
attempts. The answer is not one cause, and the largest one is not the goal.

A greedy rollout walks each induced engine's own model for up to 400 steps
(linear in depth, where the shipped BFS is exponential) and reads
is_level_complete as a passive observer. That separates three situations the
gate reports as the single verdict `goal_unreached_within_depth`:

  13/40  inert at root -- the engine predicts no action changes anything
   8/40  disproved at the engine's own dynamical fixed point
   8/40  not valid Python
   4/40  goal REACHED, at depth 61 -- past the shipped max_depth=40
   4/40  cycling; 2/40 reachable inside the horizon; 1 timeout

So 21 of 40 candidates never had a usable engine: a missing dynamics model,
not a wrong goal, is the leading cause of stall-path failure.

The 4 reaching depth 61 overturn Phase 1's headline. Phase 1 reported criterion
(iii) = 0 and explained it as an EMPTY INTERSECTION of dynamics-clean and
goal-satisfiable candidates. Re-run on the SHIPPED gate and planner with only
max_depth moved to 61 -- max_nodes held at 20000, every quality check untouched
-- three held-out-accuracy-1.0 tn36 engines go from `goal_unreached_within_depth`
to a found 61-action plan in 2229 nodes, 11% of the budget they already had.
The intersection was never empty; the depth-40 BFS could not see it. Phase 1's
yields at shipped defaults are unchanged and remain the honest description of
what the live pipeline would have done.

INDEPENDENTLY REPLICATED. A concurrent sibling session (commit 92a7ef538,
results/arc_induce_depth_20260731/) reached the same conclusion from a
separately written harness, neither session having seen the other. Agreement is
exact on quantities neither could have guessed: first depth with a non-empty
intersection 61, members {tn36 k0, k2, k6}, plan_length 61, nodes_expanded 2226.
It also shows the intersection SATURATES -- 80/120/200 add nothing over 61 --
ruling out the reading that more horizon keeps buying passes. Since this claim
overturns the preceding phase's headline, it should not have rested on one
harness; it no longer does.

The node budget was never binding, and that is measured rather than assumed:
tn36's 32 predicted-changing root actions collapse to ONE distinct successor
(the engine fills the next cell wherever the click lands), and both gate and
planner dedup by state key (REQ-ARC-WMTE-6051), so the search tree is a path.
On a path 20000 nodes buys 20000 depth and only max_depth can stop it.

This is a horizon fix, not a threshold relaxation, and the sweep proves it cuts
both ways: it also converts 3 candidates from UNDECIDED to
`degenerate_goal_predicate`. No production default was edited.

The decoupling -- can a correct dynamics engine steer exploration without a
certified goal -- is NOT supported and, honestly, not testable here. Change
prediction on the proven out-of-sample split is at chance (median balanced
accuracy 0.500, range 0.375-0.625 over 12 candidate-games; 6 are literally the
constant "nothing changes" predictor and 3 are below chance). Headroom and
capability are anti-correlated with no overlap: the games with no-op headroom
(lp85 1.00, sc25 0.93, ft09 0.80) have inert engines, and the games with working
engines (tn36, tu93) have zero headroom. No positive control exists in this
corpus, so the artifact declares FALSE_NEGATIVE_RISK and the null must not be
propagated as "dynamics-guided exploration does not work".

One hypothesis of mine was killed by its own control: inert engines are not an
action-space mismatch between the planner's centroid clicks and the tape's
coordinates. Re-probing the identical root with the tape's own actions agrees
with the planner's on every candidate.

Not verified here: whether tn36's induced goal is the TRUE win condition. Every
claim is about the engine's own model. No ARC game was played, scored or
offline, and no level was banked. The cheapest test that would settle it is
named in the artifact.

Zero GPU. adversarial_verify: 0 flagged. 10 tests, negative-controlled by
mutating the classifier and confirming the suite fails.

